  "Question": "The locus of the centers of all circles of given radius \\(a,\\) in the same plane, passing through a fixed point, is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "a point",
    "B": "a straight line",
    "C": "two straight lines",
    "D": "a circle",
    "E": "two circles"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let \\(P\\) be the fixed point, and let the given radius be \\(a>0\\). If a circle with center \\(C\\) and radius \\(a\\) passes through \\(P\\), then \\(CP=a\\).\n\nConversely, whenever \\(CP=a\\), the circle centered at \\(C\\) with radius \\(a\\) passes through \\(P\\). Thus the possible centers are exactly the points at distance \\(a\\) from \\(P\\). These points form a circle centered at \\(P\\) with radius \\(a\\), so the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
